# Artifact Preflight Gate

No kernel/CLI implementation until this triad exists for non-trivial work:

```
docs/research/<feature>.md  →  docs/specs/<feature>_spec.md  →  tasks/active/<task>.md
```

## Single-owner facts

| Fact type | Owner |
|-----------|-------|
| Metrics, phase, module list | `memories/repo/project_structure.md` |
| Identity | `VISION.md` |
| Process detail | `AWOS.md` |

Never copy numbers or phase status into research/spec — link with `[[wiki links]]`.

## Spec step shape

Each step: **one change, one test, one proof**. If description contains "and" → split.

## HTML companions

Task files and checkpoints are **Markdown-canonical** — never create an HTML companion for them. The agent's scripts (`quality_gate.py`, `obsidian_lint.py`) parse Markdown only; HTML is invisible to them.

Research and specs are Markdown-canonical too; HTML rendering is optional and only for a human who will open it. If an HTML rendering exists, keep the `.md` complete and self-contained (frontmatter + full content + `## Related` wiki links) — never a bare pointer.

## Write-gate

Decisions are not real until written in the **same turn**. No deferred "I'll add that to the spec later."
